{
  "_comment": [
    "Citation Topics per paper, read from Web of Science Core Collection through",
    "Yonsei's subscription on 2026-08-14. Clarivate's classification, built with",
    "CWTS Leiden by clustering the citation network — see data/wos-glossary.json",
    "for the official definition and link.",
    "",
    "Paper-based and single-label, which is the opposite of the subject categories",
    "in data/wos-categories.json. Each paper has exactly one micro topic, which",
    "rolls up to one meso and one macro; only the meso is stored, since the macro",
    "is its numeric prefix.",
    "",
    "The two schemes disagree, and that is the point rather than a fault. The IJCAI",
    "paper is Computer Science by venue and 2.123 Protein Structure by citation.",
    "A Protein Embedding Model for Drug Molecular Screening is 4.183 Transportation",
    "— citation clustering put a drug-screening paper among transport research.",
    "Single-label means a reader who does not open the right topic never sees the",
    "paper, so this is the weaker scheme to filter on and the better one to read.",
    "",
    "Keyed by DOI, lowercased, or exact title where there is no DOI.",
    "",
    "Ten papers have no entry: nine are absent from the Core Collection, and",
    "\"Does the Matthew effect exist in open peer review?\" is indexed but not yet",
    "assigned a topic — it was published in 2026 and clustering lags.",
    "",
    "Spelling is Clarivate's, including \"Protein Stucture\"."
  ],
